Date: Fri, 9 Jul 93 17:31:21 WET DST
From: rjc@gnu.ai.mit.edu (Ray)
Subject: Sigs again?

 1) The From: line contains the original sender. If your mail reader shows
something different it is broken.

 2) The new list software contains a command called "private". If you wish
to send a response privately to a poster, you respond to the message with
::private on the first line. If you want to send the post to multiple
people privately, you do:

::private  (goes to the person you are responding to)
::private foo@bar (adds foo@bar to the list of private recipients)
::private baz@zon (adds baz@zon to the list "    "      ")
::private user_not_on_the_extropians_list@xxx
	 (illegal, this is a security measure to prevent someone from
	  using the list as an anonymous remailer)

  This should cut down on the amount of accidental private messages
sent to the list because it takes less work (no editing reply-to, or
finding out the email address) and it is the first thing you do before
entering the message instead of the last.
(the new software is only in beta so it's not available yet for general
usage)

 3) Sigs should be kept to a minimum. net.etiquette allows 5 lines
(some versions of inews will reject more). 2 lines seems like the
most visually friendly.

